From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:11:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/34] trap-coherent surfaces behind
 surface_coherent

A surface's copy back stays deferred with its pages poisoned through a KVM-only
view: the first guest touch syncs the pending rectangles on the CPU with
VK_EXT_host_image_copy, a write opens its page and the next GPU use copies it
in, a CPU write is kept by merging against a snapshot. Off by default.

Fixes two things surface_lazy_present_all got wrong: a released texture's
completed writes were discarded while the surface stayed mapped, and CPU
readers saw stale bytes until the next flush.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
